#: src/ai/overview.md:3
msgid "AI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed is an open-source AI code editor. AI runs throughout the editing "
"experience: agents that read and write your code, inline transformations, "
"code completions on every keystroke, and conversations with models in any "
"buffer."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:7
msgid "How Zed approaches AI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:9
msgid ""
"Zed's AI features run inside a native, GPU-accelerated application built in "
"Rust. There is no Electron layer between you and the model output."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:11
msgid ""
"**Open source.** The editor and all AI features are [open source](https://"
"github.com/zed-industries/zed). You can read how AI is implemented, how data "
"flows to providers, and how tool calls execute."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:12
msgid ""
"**Multi-model.** Use Zed's hosted models or [bring your own API keys](./llm-"
"providers.md) from Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Ollama, and 8+ other "
"providers. Run local models, connect to cloud APIs, or mix both. Switch "
"models per task."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:13
msgid ""
"**External agents.** Run Claude Agent, Gemini CLI, Codex, and other CLI-"
"based agents directly in Zed through the [Agent Client Protocol](https://zed."
"dev/acp). See [External Agents](./external-agents.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:14
msgid ""
"**Privacy by default.** AI data sharing is opt-in. When you use your own API "
"keys, Zed maintains zero-data retention agreements with providers. See "
"[Privacy and Security](./privacy-and-security.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:16
msgid "Agentic editing"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:18
msgid ""
"The [Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md) is where you work with AI agents. Agents "
"can read files, edit code, run terminal commands, search the web, and access "
"diagnostics through [built-in tools](./tools.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:20
msgid ""
"You can extend agents with additional tools through [MCP servers](./mcp.md), "
"control what they can access with [tool permissions](./tool-permissions.md), "
"and shape their behavior with [rules](./rules.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:22
msgid ""
"The [Inline Assistant](./inline-assistant.md) works differently: select code "
"or a terminal command, describe what you want, and the model rewrites the "
"selection in place. It works with multiple cursors."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:24
msgid "Code completions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:26
msgid ""
"[Edit Prediction](./edit-prediction.md) provides AI code completions on "
"every keystroke. Each keypress sends a request to the prediction provider, "
"which returns single or multi-line suggestions you accept with `tab`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:28
msgid ""
"The default provider is Zeta, Zed's open-source model trained on open data. "
"You can also use GitHub Copilot, or Codestral."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:30
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:32
msgid ""
"[Configuration](./configuration.md): Connect to Anthropic, OpenAI, Ollama, "
"Google AI, or other LLM providers."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:33
msgid ""
"[External Agents](./external-agents.md): Run Claude Agent, Codex, Aider, or "
"other external agents inside Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:34
msgid "[Subscription](./subscription.md): Zed's hosted models and billing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:35
msgid ""
"[Privacy and Security](./privacy-and-security.md): How Zed handles data when "
"using AI features."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:37
msgid ""
"New to Zed? Start with [Getting Started](../getting-started.md), then come "
"back here to set up AI. For a higher-level overview, see [zed.dev/ai]"
"(https://zed.dev/ai)."
msgstr ""
